  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday Night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1055 AM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThe majority of the week is expected to feature broad ridging over\nthe eastern CONUS, which will keep temperatures 5-10 degrees \nabove normal. Despite this abnormally warm regime, it will still \nfeel quite pleasant to the average person. \"Normal\" temperatures \nfor this time of year are around 70 degrees in the afternoon, so \ntemperatures in the mid to upper 70s is anomalous but not \nuncomfortably warm. Humidity remains low through the week as well.\nWith no rain in sight through the end of the week, areawide \ndrought conditions are expected to worsen.\n\nYou'll have to look beyond the current forecast period for signs \nof a pattern shift. Long range ensembles finally hint at a \ntransition to more to a troughing regime starting next Saturday \n(Halloween). LREF probabilities of measurable rainfall (0.01\") \njump up to 30-40% Saturday night into Sunday morning. This will be\nsomething to keep an eye on for trick-or-treating night. Several \nsolutions are much later with the onset of precip on Sunday, but \nworth keeping an eye on for the few outliers Saturday afternoon.",
